---
const pains = [
  {
    icon: 'clipboard',
    title: 'Paper sign-in sheets and manual check-in',
    note: 'No instant access to medical alerts or session history',
  },
  {
    icon: 'search',
    title: 'No real-time classroom visibility',
    note: 'No way to see progress without walking the room',
  },
  {
    icon: 'phone',
    title: 'Pickup texts from personal phones',
    note: 'No automation, no consent tracking, no records',
  },
  {
    icon: 'archive',
    title: 'Student data scattered across systems',
    note: 'Some in spreadsheets, some undocumented',
  },
  {
    icon: 'users',
    title: 'Every system required one email per child',
    note: 'Families forced into duplicate accounts',
  },
];
---
<section class="section bg-cool" id="why">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <span class="script script-xl" style="color:var(--secondary-text)">Here's Why We Built This</span>
    <h2 class="headline">She didn't open her center to fight with software.</h2>
    <div class="curve curve-left"></div>
    <div class="feature-split" style="gap:3rem;align-items:start">
      <div class="origin-prose">
        <p>Our first client runs a franchise tutoring center with over 300 students. She got into education for the kids, but found herself spending more time managing broken tools than working with families.</p>
        <p>She wasn't on paper. She'd already invested in real platforms: all-in-one marketing tools, funnel builders, CRM systems that promised to handle everything. <span class="origin-highlight">Thousands of dollars</span> across multiple platforms.</p>
        <p>But every platform had the same fundamental flaw: <strong>one-to-one data relationships.</strong> One parent email, one child. A mom with three kids needed three separate accounts. That's not how families work. No amount of custom fields could fix a structural data problem.</p>
        <p>The marketing tools were great at selling online courses. The CRM systems were built for sales pipelines. None of them understood that a tutoring center has 300 students walking through a physical door. <strong>They were digital-first tools being forced into a physical-operations world.</strong></p>
        <p>So we built it differently. <strong>The Center Book starts with the database:</strong> real multi-to-multi relationships where one parent connects to multiple children, billing and communication contacts are separate, and every piece of the platform reads from the same source of truth.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-stack">
        <h3>The problems we kept seeing</h3>
        {pains.map((p) => (
          <div class="pain-item">
            <div class="pain-item-icon">
              {p.icon === 'clipboard' && (
                <svg aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#57727c" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="8" height="4" x="8" y="2" rx="1" ry="1"/><path d="M16 4h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v14a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2"/><path d="M12 11h4"/><path d="M12 16h4"/><path d="M8 11h.01"/><path d="M8 16h.01"/></svg>
              )}
              {p.icon === 'search' && (
                <svg aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#57727c" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="m21 21-4.3-4.3"/></svg>
              )}
              {p.icon === 'phone' && (
                <svg aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#57727c" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 16.92v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.18 2 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-8.63-3.07 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-3.07-8.67A2 2 0 0 1 4.11 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.72 12.84 12.84 0 0 0 .7 2.81 2 2 0 0 1-.45 2.11L8.09 9.91a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.27-1.27a2 2 0 0 1 2.11-.45 12.84 12.84 0 0 0 2.81.7A2 2 0 0 1 22 16.92z"/></svg>
              )}
              {p.icon === 'archive' && (
                <svg aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#57727c" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="20" height="5" x="2" y="3" rx="1"/><path d="M4 8v11a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8"/><path d="M10 12h4"/></svg>
              )}
              {p.icon === 'users' && (
                <svg aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#57727c" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
              )}
            </div>
            <div class="pain-item-text">
              <strong>{p.title}</strong>
              <span>{p.note}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="pain-note">
          <strong>The common thread?</strong><br><span>Great educators spending their energy on tools instead of students</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
